    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **281 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` rule on owner creation. When a new owner is created, the field is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city (both compared case-insensitively), otherwise `false`. Creation still succeeds in all cases.\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (`POST /api/owners`) \u2014 added `owner.setSharesHousehold(sharesHousehold(owner.getAddress(), owner.getCity()))` before saving, plus a `sharesHousehold(...)` helper that checks existing owners for a matching address+city (returns `false` if either field is null).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter, matching the existing field pattern. MapStruct maps it into the response DTO automatically by name.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column so the value round-trips through the DB (the value is computed at creation, stored, and read back on `GET`).\n\nThe new `Cp17Tests` acceptance test passes, and the rest of the suite remains green.",
